.TH ferry-backup 1  Ferry "Ferry Manual"
.SH NAME
ferry\-backup \- Back up this device (its key and paired devices, encrypted with a password) or restore such a backup – the same file as in the desktop and Android app
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBferry backup\fR [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Back up this device (its key and paired devices, encrypted with a password) or restore such a backup – the same file as in the desktop and Android app
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<CODE>\fR
Interface language for this run (`en`, `pl`); overrides the saved setting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ferry\-backup\-create(1)
Write a backup of the key, the name and the paired devices, encrypted with a password (asked for; from standard input when it is not a terminal)
.TP
ferry\-backup\-restore(1)
Restore a backup made here, in the desktop app or on Android: its key replaces this device\*(Aqs key (kept as a `.bak` file) and its paired devices are added
